t  not only did they feel impelled  to wage war against him but they really  thought they could win  they had this uh exaggerated view of  american power that whenever we start  something we can win  and it was that arrogance that brought  the united states into the war in  vietnam what was the source of their  anti-communism  i think it came from their  long formation as  members of the american elite and then  of course decades working to support the  power of american corporations in the  world  communist ideology was always aimed at  restricting the ability of international  corporations to work freely in many  other countries  but  there's something beyond just ideology  that i think must have driven them it's  this idea that there's always a horrible  force out there and that's why i start  my book with a quote from captain ahab  and moby dick  he says  that inscrutable thing  is chiefly what i hate and be the white  whale agent or be the white whale  principal i will wreak my hate upon him  you also write in your book about diego  rivera's  famous painting glorious victory in  which  you can see  john foster dallas  his brother right behind him with a  satchel full of money  and uh  general eisenhower down here in a bomb  why did you pick this uh and write about  it i consider this to be one of the most  brilliant works of political art of the  20th century and while i was writing  this book since the dulles brothers are  right in the middle of the picture i  decided i got to go see that picture  i've studied it of course in  reproductions over many years but i had  to go see it but i couldn't find it it  should have been in mexico we checked  with every diego rivera group finally i  tracked it down  it's in a museum in moscow  i was willing to go to moscow and i  wrote to the museum director and i got  back a note saying i'm sorry to tell you  that this picture is not on display it's  too big it's 16 feet long it's on a roll  in the basement if you come to m